#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:1
msgid "Appendix C: Derivable Traits"
msgstr "附录C：可推导出的特征"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:3
msgid ""
"In various places in the book, we’ve discussed the `derive` attribute, which "
"you can apply to a struct or enum definition. The `derive` attribute "
"generates code that will implement a trait with its own default "
"implementation on the type you’ve annotated with the `derive` syntax."
msgstr ""
"在书的各个部分中，我们讨论过`derive`属性，您可以将该属性应用于结构体或枚举类"
"型的定义。`derive`属性则会生成代码，用于在该类型上实现具有自定义默认实现的特"
"征。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:8
msgid ""
"In this appendix, we provide a reference of all the traits in the standard "
"library that you can use with `derive`. Each section covers:"
msgstr ""
"在这个附录中，我们提供了标准库中所有可以与`derive`一起使用的特性的参考。每个"
"部分都涵盖了以下内容："

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:11
msgid "What operators and methods deriving this trait will enable"
msgstr "哪些操作符和方法能够启用此特性"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:12
msgid "What the implementation of the trait provided by `derive` does"
msgstr "`derive`所提供的特性实现内容是什么"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:13
msgid "What implementing the trait signifies about the type"
msgstr "实现该特性对类型有何意义"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:14
msgid ""
"The conditions in which you’re allowed or not allowed to implement the trait"
msgstr "在哪些情况下可以或不可以实现该特性"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:15
msgid "Examples of operations that require the trait"
msgstr "需要使用该特性的操作示例"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:17
msgid ""
"If you want different behavior from that provided by the `derive` attribute, "
"consult the [standard library documentation](../std/index.html)<!-- ignore --"
"> for each trait for details on how to manually implement them."
msgstr ""
"如果您希望获得与 ``derive`` 属性所提供的行为不同的结果，请查阅[标准库文档]"
"(../std/index.html)中的相关说明，了解如何手动实现这些功能的具体方法。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:21
msgid ""
"The traits listed here are the only ones defined by the standard library "
"that can be implemented on your types using `derive`. Other traits defined "
"in the standard library don’t have sensible default behavior, so it’s up to "
"you to implement them in the way that makes sense for what you’re trying to "
"accomplish."
msgstr ""
"这里列出的特性是标准库中唯一可以通过`derive`在你的类型上实现的特性。标准库中"
"定义的其他特性并没有合理的默认行为，因此你需要根据自己的需求来合理地实现它"
"们。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:26
msgid ""
"An example of a trait that can’t be derived is `Display`, which handles "
"formatting for end users. You should always consider the appropriate way to "
"display a type to an end user. What parts of the type should an end user be "
"allowed to see? What parts would they find relevant? What format of the data "
"would be most relevant to them? The Rust compiler doesn’t have this insight, "
"so it can’t provide appropriate default behavior for you."
msgstr ""
"一个无法被派生的特性的例子是`Display`，它负责处理最终用户的格式设置问题。在向"
"最终用户展示某个类型时，你应该始终考虑合适的展示方式。最终用户应该能够看到该"
"类型的哪些部分？他们认为哪些部分是相关的？哪种数据格式对他们来说最为重要？"
"Rust编译器并没有这种洞察力，因此无法为你提供适当的默认行为。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:33
msgid ""
"The list of derivable traits provided in this appendix is not comprehensive: "
"Libraries can implement `derive` for their own traits, making the list of "
"traits you can use `derive` with truly open ended. Implementing `derive` "
"involves using a procedural macro, which is covered in the [“Custom `derive` "
"Macros”](ch20-05-macros.html#custom-derive-macros)<!-- ignore --> section in "
"Chapter 20."
msgstr ""
"本附录中提供的可派生特性列表并不全面：  \n"
"库可以为其自身特性实现 ``derive``，这使得可以与 ``derive`` 结合使用的特性数量"
"变得非常广泛。而实现 ``derive`` 则需要使用过程式宏，相关内容将在第20章的[“自"
"定义 ``derive`` 宏”](ch20-05-macros.html#custom-derive-macros)<!-- 忽略 -->部"
"分进行介绍。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:39
msgid "`Debug` for Programmer Output"
msgstr "`Debug` 供程序员输出使用"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:41
msgid ""
"The `Debug` trait enables debug formatting in format strings, which you "
"indicate by adding `:?` within `{}` placeholders."
msgstr ""
"``Debug``特性使得在格式字符串中能够启用调试格式化功能，您可以通过在``{}``占位"
"符中添加``:?``来实现这一点。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:44
msgid ""
"The `Debug` trait allows you to print instances of a type for debugging "
"purposes, so you and other programmers using your type can inspect an "
"instance at a particular point in a program’s execution."
msgstr ""
"``Debug``特性允许您打印某个类型的实例，以便于调试。这样，您和其他使用该类型的"
"程序员可以在程序执行的特定阶段检查该实例。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:48
msgid ""
"The `Debug` trait is required, for example, in the use of the `assert_eq!` "
"macro. This macro prints the values of instances given as arguments if the "
"equality assertion fails so that programmers can see why the two instances "
"weren’t equal."
msgstr ""
"需要使用`Debug`特性，例如在调用`assert_eq!`宏时。当相等性断言失败时，该宏会打"
"印作为参数传递的实例的值，这样程序员就能了解为什么这两个实例并不相等。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:53
msgid "`PartialEq` and `Eq` for Equality Comparisons"
msgstr "用于相等性比较的`PartialEq`和`Eq`"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:55
msgid ""
"The `PartialEq` trait allows you to compare instances of a type to check for "
"equality and enables use of the `==` and `!=` operators."
msgstr ""
"`PartialEq`特性允许您比较同一类型的实例以检查其相等性，并使得可以使用`==`和`!"
"=`运算符。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:58
msgid ""
"Deriving `PartialEq` implements the `eq` method. When `PartialEq` is derived "
"on structs, two instances are equal only if _all_ fields are equal, and the "
"instances are not equal if _any_ fields are not equal. When derived on "
"enums, each variant is equal to itself and not equal to the other variants."
msgstr ""
"派生出的`PartialEq`实现了`eq`方法。当在结构体上派生`PartialEq`时，只有当所有"
"字段都相等时，两个实例才相等；如果有任何字段不相等，则这两个实例就不相等。而"
"当在枚举类型上进行派生时，每个变体都等于自身，而不等于其他变体。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:63
msgid ""
"The `PartialEq` trait is required, for example, with the use of the "
"`assert_eq!` macro, which needs to be able to compare two instances of a "
"type for equality."
msgstr ""
"需要使用`PartialEq`特性，例如，通过使用`assert_eq!`宏，该宏需要能够比较两个类"
"型的实例是否相等。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:67
msgid ""
"The `Eq` trait has no methods. Its purpose is to signal that for every value "
"of the annotated type, the value is equal to itself. The `Eq` trait can only "
"be applied to types that also implement `PartialEq`, although not all types "
"that implement `PartialEq` can implement `Eq`. One example of this is "
"floating-point number types: The implementation of floating-point numbers "
"states that two instances of the not-a-number (`NaN`) value are not equal to "
"each other."
msgstr ""
"`Eq`特性没有方法。其目的是为了表明注释类型的每个值都等于自己。 `Eq`特性只能应"
"用于实现`PartialEq`的类型，尽管并非所有实现`PartialEq`的类型都能实现`Eq`。 这"
"方面的一个例子是浮点数类型：浮点数的实现表示两个非数字(“NAN”)值的实例不等于对"
"方。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:74
msgid ""
"An example of when `Eq` is required is for keys in a `HashMap<K, V>` so that "
"the `HashMap<K, V>` can tell whether two keys are the same."
msgstr ""
"一个需要使用`Eq`的例子是出现在`HashMap<K, V>`中的键，这样`HashMap<K, V>`就能"
"判断两个键是否相同。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:77
msgid "`PartialOrd` and `Ord` for Ordering Comparisons"
msgstr "用于排序比较的 `PartialOrd` 和 `Ord`"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:79
msgid ""
"The `PartialOrd` trait allows you to compare instances of a type for sorting "
"purposes. A type that implements `PartialOrd` can be used with the `<`, `>`, "
"`<=`, and `>=` operators. You can only apply the `PartialOrd` trait to types "
"that also implement `PartialEq`."
msgstr ""
"`PartialOrd`特性允许您为了排序的目的而比较同一类型的实例。实现了`PartialOrd`"
"的类型可以与`<`、`>`、`<=`以及`>=`运算符一起使用。您只能将`PartialOrd`特性应"
"用于同时实现了`PartialEq`的类型。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:84
msgid ""
"Deriving `PartialOrd` implements the `partial_cmp` method, which returns an "
"`Option<Ordering>` that will be `None` when the values given don’t produce "
"an ordering. An example of a value that doesn’t produce an ordering, even "
"though most values of that type can be compared, is the `NaN` floating point "
"value. Calling `partial_cmp` with any floating-point number and the `NaN` "
"floating-point value will return `None`."
msgstr ""
"调用 `PartialOrd` 会执行 `partial_cmp` 方法，该方法返回一个 "
"`Option<Ordering>` 值。当给定的值无法产生排序时，该值将被转换为 `None`。一个"
"无法产生排序的例子是 `NaN` 浮点数值。无论使用哪个浮点数值以及 `NaN` 浮点数"
"值，调用 `partial_cmp` 都会返回 `None`。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:91
msgid ""
"When derived on structs, `PartialOrd` compares two instances by comparing "
"the value in each field in the order in which the fields appear in the "
"struct definition. When derived on enums, variants of the enum declared "
"earlier in the enum definition are considered less than the variants listed "
"later."
msgstr ""
"在结构体上派生时，``PartialOrd``通过按照结构体定义中字段出现的顺序来比较两个"
"实例中的各个字段的值。在枚举上派生时，枚举定义中较早声明的枚举变体会被视为比"
"后面列出的变体更不优先。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:96
msgid ""
"The `PartialOrd` trait is required, for example, for the `gen_range` method "
"from the `rand` crate that generates a random value in the range specified "
"by a range expression."
msgstr ""
"需要`PartialOrd`特性，例如，在`gen_range`方法中。该方法来自`rand`框架，该框架"
"能够生成由范围表达式指定的范围内的随机值。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:100
msgid ""
"The `Ord` trait allows you to know that for any two values of the annotated "
"type, a valid ordering will exist. The `Ord` trait implements the `cmp` "
"method, which returns an `Ordering` rather than an `Option<Ordering>` "
"because a valid ordering will always be possible. You can only apply the "
"`Ord` trait to types that also implement `PartialOrd` and `Eq` (and `Eq` "
"requires `PartialEq`). When derived on structs and enums, `cmp` behaves the "
"same way as the derived implementation for `partial_cmp` does with "
"`PartialOrd`."
msgstr ""
"`Ord` 特性允许你确定，对于任何两个被标注的类型值来说，总存在一种有效的排序方"
"式。`Ord` 特性实现了 `cmp` 方法，该方法返回的是 `Ordering` 而不是 "
"`Option<Ordering>`，因为总是可以找到一个有效的排序方式。你只能将 `Ord` 特性应"
"用于那些同时实现了 `PartialOrd` 和 `Eq` 的类型（而 `Eq` 则需要 "
"`PartialEq`）。在结构体和集合类型中派生时，``cmp``的行为与``partial_cmp``的"
"`derivedimplementation`对``PartialOrd``的行为相同。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:108
msgid ""
"An example of when `Ord` is required is when storing values in a "
"`BTreeSet<T>`, a data structure that stores data based on the sort order of "
"the values."
msgstr ""
"当需要`Ord`时，一个例子是当将值存储在`BTreeSet<T>`时， 基于值排序的数据结构储"
"存数据。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:111
msgid "`Clone` and `Copy` for Duplicating Values"
msgstr "用于复制值的 `Clone` 和 `Copy`"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:113
msgid ""
"The `Clone` trait allows you to explicitly create a deep copy of a value, "
"and the duplication process might involve running arbitrary code and copying "
"heap data. See the [“Variables and Data Interacting with Clone”](ch04-01-"
"what-is-ownership.html#variables-and-data-interacting-with-clone)<!-- ignore "
"--> section in Chapter 4 for more information on `Clone`."
msgstr ""
"``Clone``特性允许您显式地创建一个值的深度复制，而复制过程可能涉及运行任意代码"
"以及复制堆数据。有关``Clone``的更多信息，请参阅第4章中的[“变量与数据在克隆中"
"的交互”](ch04-01-what-is-ownership.html#variables-and-data-interacting-with-"
"clone)<!-- 忽略 -->部分。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:119
msgid ""
"Deriving `Clone` implements the `clone` method, which when implemented for "
"the whole type, calls `clone` on each of the parts of the type. This means "
"all the fields or values in the type must also implement `Clone` to derive "
"`Clone`."
msgstr ""
"派生`Clone`实现了`clone`方法，当实现整个类型时，在类型的每个部分上调用 "
"`clone` 方法。 这意味着类型中的所有字段或值都必须实现 `Clone` 才能找到 "
"`Clone` 。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:123
msgid ""
"An example of when `Clone` is required is when calling the `to_vec` method "
"on a slice. The slice doesn’t own the type instances it contains, but the "
"vector returned from `to_vec` will need to own its instances, so `to_vec` "
"calls `clone` on each item. Thus, the type stored in the slice must "
"implement `Clone`."
msgstr ""
"当需要`Clone`时，一个例子是在切片上调用 `to_vec` 方法。 切片不拥有它包含的类"
"型实例， 但从`to_vec`返回的矢量将需要拥有其实例，所以`to_vec`在每个项目上调用"
"`clone`。 因此，切片中存储的类型必须实现 `Clone'。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:128
msgid ""
"The `Copy` trait allows you to duplicate a value by only copying bits stored "
"on the stack; no arbitrary code is necessary. See the [“Stack-Only Data: "
"Copy”](ch04-01-what-is-ownership.html#stack-only-data-copy)<!-- ignore --> "
"section in Chapter 4 for more information on `Copy`."
msgstr ""
"``Copy``特性允许您通过仅复制存储在栈上的数据来复制一个值；无需编写任何自定义"
"代码。有关``Copy``的更多信息，请参阅第4章中的(ch04-01-what-is-ownership."
"html#stack-only-data-copy)部分。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:133
msgid ""
"The `Copy` trait doesn’t define any methods to prevent programmers from "
"overloading those methods and violating the assumption that no arbitrary "
"code is being run. That way, all programmers can assume that copying a value "
"will be very fast."
msgstr ""
"`Copy`这个特性并没有定义任何方法来防止程序员过度使用这些方法，从而避免违反“不"
"会运行任意代码”的假设。这样一来，所有程序员都可以认为复制一个值的过程会非常快"
"速。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:138
msgid ""
"You can derive `Copy` on any type whose parts all implement `Copy`. A type "
"that implements `Copy` must also implement `Clone` because a type that "
"implements `Copy` has a trivial implementation of `Clone` that performs the "
"same task as `Copy`."
msgstr ""
"你可以将`Copy`应用于任何其所有部分都实现了`Copy`的类型。一个实现了`Copy`的类"
"型也必须实现`Clone`，因为一个实现了`Copy`的类型有一个简单的实现方式来实现"
"`Clone`，而这个实现方式与`Copy`所执行的任务相同。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:143
msgid ""
"The `Copy` trait is rarely required; types that implement `Copy` have "
"optimizations available, meaning you don’t have to call `clone`, which makes "
"the code more concise."
msgstr ""
"`Copy`特性很少被需要；实现了`Copy`的类型具有优化功能，这意味着不必调用"
"`clone`，从而使代码更加简洁。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:147
msgid ""
"Everything possible with `Copy` you can also accomplish with `Clone`, but "
"the code might be slower or have to use `clone` in places."
msgstr ""
"使用`Copy`可以完成所有可能的事情，你也可以使用`Clone`来实现同样的功能，不过代"
"码可能会运行得较慢，或者在某些地方需要使用`clone`。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:150
msgid "`Hash` for Mapping a Value to a Value of Fixed Size"
msgstr "`Hash` 用于将值映射到固定大小的值"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:152
msgid ""
"The `Hash` trait allows you to take an instance of a type of arbitrary size "
"and map that instance to a value of fixed size using a hash function. "
"Deriving `Hash` implements the `hash` method. The derived implementation of "
"the `hash` method combines the result of calling `hash` on each of the parts "
"of the type, meaning all fields or values must also implement `Hash` to "
"derive `Hash`."
msgstr ""
"`Hash`特性允许您获取一个任意大小的类型实例，并使用哈希函数将该实例映射为固定"
"大小的值。`Hash`实现了`hash`方法。`hash`的派生实现会调用`hash`来处理类型的每"
"个部分，这意味着所有字段或值也必须实现`Hash`才能推导出`Hash`。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:158
msgid ""
"An example of when `Hash` is required is in storing keys in a `HashMap<K, "
"V>` to store data efficiently."
msgstr ""
"在存储键时使用`Hash`的一个例子是在`HashMap<K, V>`中，以便高效存储数据。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:161
msgid "`Default` for Default Values"
msgstr "`Default` 用于默认值"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:163
msgid ""
"The `Default` trait allows you to create a default value for a type. "
"Deriving `Default` implements the `default` function. The derived "
"implementation of the `default` function calls the `default` function on "
"each part of the type, meaning all fields or values in the type must also "
"implement `Default` to derive `Default`."
msgstr ""
"`Default` 特性允许您为某个类型创建一个默认值。`Default` 实现了 `default` 函"
"数。`default` 函数的派生实现会调用 `default` 函数来处理该类型的每个部分，这意"
"味着该类型中的所有字段或值也必须实现 `Default` 才能派生出 `Default`。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:169
msgid ""
"The `Default::default` function is commonly used in combination with the "
"struct update syntax discussed in the [“Creating Instances from Other "
"Instances with Struct Update Syntax”](ch05-01-defining-structs.html#creating-"
"instances-from-other-instances-with-struct-update-syntax)<!--\n"
"ignore --> section in Chapter 5. You can customize a few fields of a struct "
"and then set and use a default value for the rest of the fields by using `.."
"Default::default()`."
msgstr ""
"`Default::default`函数通常与在第五章的(ch05-01-defining-structs."
"html#creating-instances-from-other-instances-with-struct-update-syntax)"
"[creating-instances-from-other-instances-with-struct-update-syntax]节中讨论的"
"结构更新语法一起使用。您可以通过使用`..Default::default()`来自定义结构的某些"
"字段，并为其余字段设置并使用默认值。"

#: src/appendix-03-derivable-traits.md:177
msgid ""
"The `Default` trait is required when you use the method `unwrap_or_default` "
"on `Option<T>` instances, for example. If the `Option<T>` is `None`, the "
"method `unwrap_or_default` will return the result of `Default::default` for "
"the type `T` stored in the `Option<T>`."
msgstr ""
"例如，当您在`Option<T>`实例上使用`unwrap_or_default`方法时，需要引入`Default`"
"特性。如果`Option<T>`等于`None`，那么`unwrap_or_default`方法将返回存储在"
"`Option<T>`中的`T`类型的`Default::default`的结果。"
